zonaro-nautilus-extensions
==========================

This directory is the system payload for the zonaro Nautilus extensions.

Every extension package installs its Python module(s) here.  Because Nautilus
Python only loads extensions from the per-user directory, the shared helper
/usr/bin/zonaro-nautilus-link (shipped by zonaro-nautilus-common) symlinks the
contents of this directory into:

    ~/.local/share/nautilus-python/extensions/

The linker runs automatically at session start through the XDG autostart entry
/etc/xdg/autostart/zonaro-nautilus-link.desktop.

Extensions disabled with the Extensions Manager are moved to the "disabled/"
subfolder of the per-user directory and are skipped by the linker, so the
choice is preserved across logins.

Do not edit the files in this directory by hand: they are managed by apt.
